0..76 Comment "// An owned string ends in one zero byte, so a C function reads its bytes as"
77..153 Comment "// they are held: the owned string is already the C string, with no copy and"
154..232 Comment "// no re-encoding at the boundary (the C standard\'s string, ISO/IEC 9899:2018,"
233..310 Comment "// § 7.1.1; Rust\'s `CStr` is the borrowed form of the same layout). A string"
311..389 Comment "// with a zero inside it has no C reading, and the boundary says so instead of"
390..410 Comment "// cutting it short."
412..460 Comment "// The lists; the byte lists; the UTF-8 encoder."
